ut': 'Evaluation: The current board position shows that Black has several "Sleeping 3" lines (I7-J8-K9, I11-J10-K9, J8-J9-J10) but all are blocked on one end, preventing an immediate win. However, the most critical feature of the board is the opponent\'s (White) threat. White has stones at L8 and L10 with a gap at L9. If White plays L9, they will form a vertical "Live 3" (L8-L9-L10) because L7 and L11 are empty. A "Live 3" allows White to create a "Live 4" or "Split 4" on the next turn, guaranteeing a win unless Black has an immediate VCF (Victory by Continuous Fours). Analysis of Black\'s forcing moves (H6, H12, J7) reveals no continuous winning sequence. Therefore, Black must play defensively to block White\'s threat.\n\nReason: White threatens to play L9 to create a "Live 3" (L8-L9-L10), which is a winning setup. Black must block this critical square. Playing L9 not only prevents White\'s win but also connects Black\'s stones at J9 and K9 to form a 3-in-a-row (J9-K9-L9), creating a counter-threat (threat to make a closed 4 at M9).\n\nAnswer: {"col": "L", "row": 9}'}
